      "side": 1,
      "message": "In (now obsolete) PS10 it wouldn\u0027t, because dexpreopt.config was only generated for non-host non-test libraries (not all execution paths reach dexpreopt() in compile() for java.Module), and it has to be kept in sync with generation of LOCAL_SOONG_DEXPREOPT_CONFIG variable for Make, otherwise `m checkbuild` detects dangling build targets.\n\nIn PS11 I rewrote this to set the config path once at the time when the build rule for dexpreopt.config is generated, for it cannot get out of sync with LOCAL_SOONG_DEXPREOPT_CONFIG anymore. Some build rules for dexpreopt.config may be redundant, but this was the case anyway as it\u0027s impossible to know which Make modules will depend on it (if any). I think it\u0027s too much of a hassle to prune the redundant build rules.\n\nThat is all in the assumption that PS11 passes presubmit (checkbuild), which is slow for me today for some reason.",
      "parentUuid": "297283f0_026f57d2",
